From 232bc754af1ff321c1edf59e8b9358bf11d761cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hauke Mehrtens <hauke@hauke-m.de>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 22:56:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] kernel: netfilter: fix flow offload with an unknown
 forward path

6.18.45 pulled in b5964aac51e0 ("netfilter: flowtable: consolidate xmit
path") as a dependency of the CVE fix 8aecf0bbcc72. Since then the
FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH path no longer transmits on the dst device, it
looks the output device up by flow_offload_tuple.ifidx, which is fed from
route->tuple[dir].out.ifindex.

That field is only assigned in nft_dev_forward_path() when the forward
path could be discovered, nft_default_forward_path() never sets it. A
flow whose egress path cannot be resolved is therefore offloaded with an
interface index of 0, nf_flow_offload_ip_hook() drops the packet and
tears the flow down, the flow_offload expression offloads it again right
away and the loss repeats instead of settling.

Bridged Wi-Fi is the common case: mac80211 fails .ndo_fill_forward_path
with -EOPNOTSUPP unless the driver implements .net_fill_forward_path, and
with WED the path ends in DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA, which the parser does not
handle either, so both ways end up without an output device. This matches
the reports of sporadic packet loss towards wireless clients with
software flow offloading enabled on mediatek/filogic.

Add a patch that falls back to the dst device, which is the device the
neighbour is looked up on and the device the packets were transmitted on
before the xmit paths were merged. Mainline avoids the situation
differently since 871df5007eda ("netfilter: flowtable: bail out if
forward path cannot be discovered"), which sits on top of the forward
path discovery rework and does not apply to 6.18.y. 6.12 does not carry
the rework and is not affected.

Fixes: da5c83ece675 ("kernel: bump 6.18 to 6.18.45")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Hauke Mehrtens <hauke@hauke-m.de>
---
 ...ble-set-out-ifindex-when-the-forward.patch | 59 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 59 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/699-netfilter-flowtable-set-out-ifindex-when-the-forward.patch

diff --git a/target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/699-netfilter-flowtable-set-out-ifindex-when-the-forward.patch b/target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/699-netfilter-flowtable-set-out-ifindex-when-the-forward.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000000..aa250063b95279
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/699-netfilter-flowtable-set-out-ifindex-when-the-forward.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+From: Hauke Mehrtens <hauke@hauke-m.de>
+Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 22:15:00 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: set out ifindex when the forward path
+ is unknown
+
+Since commit b5964aac51e0 ("netfilter: flowtable: consolidate xmit path")
+the FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH path does not transmit on the dst device any
+more, it looks the output device up by the interface index stored in the
+flow tuple:
+
+	xmit.outdev = dev_get_by_index_rcu(state->net, tuplehash->tuple.ifidx);
+	if (!xmit.outdev) {
+		flow_offload_teardown(flow);
+		return NF_DROP;
+	}
+
+That index comes from route->tuple[dir].out.ifindex, which is only
+assigned in nft_dev_forward_path() when the forward path could be
+discovered.  nft_default_forward_path() never sets it, so a flow whose
+egress path cannot be resolved is offloaded with an interface index of 0.
+Every packet of such a flow is then dropped while the flow entry is torn
+down, and the flow_offload expression offloads it again right away, so
+the loss repeats instead of settling.
+
+This is easy to hit on a router that bridges Wi-Fi and Ethernet:
+mac80211 returns -EOPNOTSUPP from .ndo_fill_forward_path when the driver
+does not implement .net_fill_forward_path, and dev_fill_forward_path()
+turns any error into a failure of the whole path lookup.  Traffic towards
+Wi-Fi clients then loses a packet per re-offload cycle, which shows up as
+sporadic stalls and lost UDP datagrams rather than as a hard failure.
+
+Fall back to the dst device, which is the device the neighbour is looked
+up on and the device the packet was transmitted on before the two xmit
+paths were merged.
+
+Mainline avoids the situation differently since commit 871df5007eda
+("netfilter: flowtable: bail out if forward path cannot be discovered"),
+which refuses to offload the flow at all.  That change sits on top of the
+forward path discovery rework and does not apply to 6.18.y, and it also
+gives up the offload for flows that were offloaded successfully before,
+so restoring the previous behaviour is the minimal fix here.
+
+Fixes: b5964aac51e0 ("netfilter: flowtable: consolidate xmit path")
+Signed-off-by: Hauke Mehrtens <hauke@hauke-m.de>
+---
+ net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c | 2 ++
+ 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)
+
+--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
++++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
+@@ -205,6 +205,8 @@ static void nft_dev_forward_path(struct
+ 
+ 	if (info.outdev)
+ 		route->tuple[dir].out.ifindex = info.outdev->ifindex;
++	else
++		route->tuple[dir].out.ifindex = dst->dev->ifindex;
+ 
+ 	if (!info.indev || !nft_flowtable_find_dev(info.indev, ft))
+ 		return;

